---
code: cli-flag-requires-mode
when-fires: a flag scoped to one invocation was given under another (or its required companion was omitted). cli/lib.rs. {flag} and the {mode} it belongs to.
why: the flag surface is per-invocation, so accepting it elsewhere would imply a capability that mode does not have.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc why --host=web1 --book=webhost.sh
dorc: error[cli-flag-requires-mode]: The `--host` flag is only valid with dorc
plan or dorc apply.
usage: dorc [probe|plan|apply] --book=<book.sh> [--pre-source <sh>]... [--debug-argv]

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: cli-flag-requires-mode
{{flag}} = "--host"
{{mode}} = "dorc\nplan or dorc apply"
